}}|position={{W|Left-wing politics|Left}} to {{W|Far-left politics|Far-left}}|religion=|national=|european=|continental=<!-- or | continental affiliation = -->|international=|europarl=|affiliation1_title=|affiliation1=|affiliation2_title=|affiliation2=|colors=<!-- or | colours = ; use based on [[WP:ENGVAR]]-->|slogan=|anthem=|blank1_title=|blank1=|blank2_title=|blank2=|blank3_title=|blank3=|blank4_title=|blank4=|seats1_title=[[Confederal Congress]]|seats1={{Composition bar|0|736|#CD1025}}|seats2_title=[[Regions of Balisca|Regional boards]]|seats2={{Composition bar|1268|24668|#CD1025}}|seats3_title=[[Cantons of Balisca|Cantonal councils]]|seats3={{Composition bar|8293|425246|#CD1025}}|seats4_title=[[Communes of Balisca|Communal councils]]|seats4={{Composition bar|121712|2027484|#CD1025}}|symbol=|website=|state=<!-- or | country = -->|country=Balisca|country_dab1=|parties_dab1=|elections_dab1=|country2=|country_dab2=|parties_dab2=|elections_dab2=|footnotes=}}The '''Kadarist Party''' ({{lang-bl|Parti Kadarista}}) is a Baliscan [[W:Platformism|platform]] established to support the confederal abandonment of [[W:Armed neutrality|armed neutrality]] and embrace of [[W:proletarian internationalism|proletarian internationalism]]. It advocates for confederal support for revolutionary parties and movements and [[W:Wars of national liberation|wars of national liberation]] across the world, including through [[Baliscan military internationalism|military internationalism or direct intervention]].

It rejects the concept of [[W:Peaceful coexistence|peaceful coexistence]], asserting that it has been repeatedly proven that "capitalism anywhere is a threat to socialism everywhere", and supported the [[Socialist Reapproachment|reconciliation of the Socialist Bloc]]. The Party emerged from a schism within the [[Revolutionary Front]] in 1981 due to it's support for the [[Kuluba Accords]], which ended the [[Camboriú War|armed conflict]] between Balisca and [[Potocsí]].

It competes with the [[Revolutionary Workers' Front]], with it's voter base being largely concentrated in rural and Indigenous communities, mostly in the [[Marañón basin]].

